SSH - run a command on another computer
Usage: ssh <computer id> <command>

Connects to another CloverOS machine over rednet, prompts for the remote
user's password, runs the command there, prints the output, closes the
session. The remote machine serves connections when its sshd unit runs:

  systemctl start sshd        (on the remote machine)

Failed logins are journaled on the server; sessions time out after five
idle minutes.

Examples:
  ssh 12 df
  ssh 3 "cat /etc/motd"
